Our technical architecture is based on the Atelier platform, a Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) platform hosted on OuraneCloud's SecNumCloud-qualified infrastructure, ensuring data sovereignty and minimizing dependency on non-European suppliers. The Atelier platform provides components for an intelligent assistance tool, including document ingestion, vector store, retrieval layer, orchestration layer, and answer layer. Its model-agnostic design allows us to choose a sovereign European open-weight model that is fully auditable and has strong grounding and citation behavior.

To ensure quick access to reliable information and response times below 2 seconds, we leverage the platform's high-performance capabilities, with median latency of 1.3 seconds and p95 latency below 2.5 seconds. The Atelier platform also supports horizontal scaling to handle peak loads during business hours, ensuring high availability. For integration with the firm's production tools, our API-first design approach using REST and webhooks enables seamless embedding in existing work environments.

We implement single sign-on (SSO) using SAML or OIDC and integrate with user directories such as LDAP or Entra ID, ensuring secure access control and auditing capabilities per client file. Our solution also supports GDPR compliance through configurable retention aligned with legal archival obligations, Role-Based Access Control (RBAC), audit logging of access and system outputs, and the appointment of a Data Protection Officer (DPO).

Our company maintains regulatory compliance through its Security & Compliance function, which monitors obligations such as GDPR, professional secrecy, anti-money-laundering frameworks, and auditor-independence rules. We are compliant with GDPR requirements, including Article 28 processing agreements, and comply with anti-money-laundering obligations and statutory-audit review requirements.

We design an AI-powered solution by leveraging the Atelier platform's Retrieval-augmented generation capabilities to provide drafting assistance through template-guided drafting. This enables the generation of client letters, mission notes, and file syntheses based on validated material from our controlled corpus. We utilize structured extraction capability with source linking, allowing for the extraction of relevant figures and information from documents while maintaining links to their original source passages.

Our solution prioritizes the principle of treating the reliability of numeric outputs as a first-class requirement, grounding figure-bearing statements in source documents and configuring the platform to refrain from producing ungrounded numeric claims. Explainability features, including source citations, retrieved passages, retrieval trace, and interaction logging, provide transparency and enable human oversight.

